    "body": "Can you add unit test cases to ensure this works and continues to do so - maybe based off the sample code you show asserting that the copy looks/works like expected.\r\n\r\nCan you also add a reno release not for this fix.\r\n\r\nAs long as the getter is used, normal for external users then this works out albeit it that it corrects the error later. Internally the code often directly accesses the _num_qubits variable - by fixing the mismatch later are we exposing ourselves to possible future bugs if code is added and uses the _num_qubits var directly. Can the mismatch be fixed earlier say by overriding copy and calling  super then fixing up the copy before returning it. This would then not have the circuit be in some inconsistent state until the getter is called.",
